{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/419418-silent-imperative-and-divine-artificer","id":419418,"title":"Silent Imperative and Divine Artificer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-25T15:26:57-08:00","id":419418,"title":"Silent Imperative and Divine Artificer","content":"so I came to the conclusion that I could either keep throwing hints, or make a whole thread about them- so here is the thread!<br /> <br /> for those who didn't noticed, those two groups are compacts presented in the Dark Eras Hunter chapter. While they don't have a lot of word count (the Divine Artificer is no more then a line), I did found their concepts as interesting- the Silent Imperative being a well connected group of hunters who help the innocents to escape unjust punishment while the Divine Artificer are zealots who both demons and their kin. Now that I have finished with the major part my Endowment for All thread, and posted most of my conspiracy ideas, I have thought maybe to start and develop those two.<br /> <br /> So- does anyone have suggestions/ ideas/ their own write ups to save me some work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:34:44-08:00","id":419528,"title":"","content":"For the Imperative, maybe give them a link to the Underworld, since they snuck people out using Catacombs? Maybe also link them to the Hedge and the Twilight, with an Endowment focused on allowing them to better use these &quot;Silent Paths&quot; to move between places?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:58:37-08:00","id":419553,"title":"","content":"The majority of agents of the Silent Imperative were, of course, less-known or more socially adept members of the most afflicted compacts and conspiracies. For the long-term health of humanity, the protection of the treasured knowledge of the vigil, and the necessity of saving the lives of their respected colleagues and friends, the vigil proper was put on hold to save the spark of the candle, itself. <br /> <br /> The Silent Imperative, however, was founded of desperation and misery, and misery acquaints a (wo)man with strange bedfellows. When the hammer was being brought down upon the Lucifuge, the beasts they hunted reacted in different ways. Some took the predictable reaction: They sought to point out where the desperate hunters were hiding, and laugh as the vigil ate itself. Others, however, took a different view of things. They offered their &quot;help&quot; to their enemy.<br /> <br /> And so, some of the monsters came bearing pacts and treaties to be signed. The continued existence of your vigil for a magically binding pledge. And of course,<br /> <br /> This was influenced, of course, by the deadly internal politics of their monster societies. It had long been a practice for one vampire cult to leave behind clues that helped the vigil track down a rival cult, after all. Even when conspiracies had the wherewithal to discern who the source of their anonymous tips, that still didn't mean they would always turn it down: Even if it helps another monster, those were often the best chances the Vigil ever had for truly decisive blows against their enemy that could spare innocents the fangs of the predators for years to come. Some offered their aegis in exchange for their word not to harm the monster's own operation while being fed the opportunity to hunt the monster's competitors. <br /> <br /> Still other monsters still bore more seemingly equitable, but even more deadly divisive offers. A few groups of monsters, arguing themselves not really monsters at all, offered services that could greatly help a vigil &quot;as acts of goodwill to fellow Christians on the long and difficult road to salvation&quot;. The Knights of St. Collen are a (not officially recognized) group of Catholic fae creatures that proffered assistance to the Lucifuge, and other Catholic-affiliated hunter groups facing persecution during this time. The fae offered passage on their &quot;trods&quot;, and through them, a mysterious land route that could take a man in a hurry across the English Channel without a boat in just hours... provided you were very, VERY careful about the guide you took with you. That they could not by any means guarantee the safety of the passage, however, was of pressing concern to all but the most desperate. For those most desperate, however, their dread power to open a door from even a blind alleyway surrounded by a lynch mob to <i>anywhere</i> else, no matter how hostile the intervening terrain, was a gamble worth taking.<br /> <br /> Other groups, including some sort of semi-splinter group of witches representing some form of Enlightenment ideal, and fashioning itself after trade guilds, offered their own services, hoping that it might establish some sort of peace between &quot;good witches&quot; and hunters, that they may focus upon the &quot;bad witches&quot;. They couched this, however, in the haughty talk of &quot;awakening&quot; a great witch congregation, as though the propagation of this blasphemy would be a blessing for mankind. <br /> <br /> Even if these free agents, or even outright would-be members of the Silent Imperative could be trusted (and the likes of the maddened fae or the infinitely duplicitous witch guilds could most certainly not be trusted without very potent and very <i>personal</i> assurances), then the suspicion that would fall upon any Hunter that dared ally with the monsters would almost certainly be as deadly as any betrayal. <br /> <br /> In the modern era, it has seemed peculiar to the agents of the Lucifuge that the Lucifuge herself sees Changelings as nothing of concern, even when they seem content to wreak havoc upon the minds of innocents for their twisted games, but will suddenly switch course of action when one of the greater Fae appear, these so-called Changeling Gentry. It's almost like she willingly plays to their own internal struggles...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}